<% # Shown only to a visitor who got here without an account, after they can
   # already see their results. The order matters: the product has to have
   # worked before it asks for anything.
   #
   # @anonymous_search is set by lib/search_routes.rb on the anonymous
   # availability route and nowhere else, so the authenticated flow never
   # renders any of this. %>
<div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
  <div id="save-results-card" class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/40">
    <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-2">Want to keep these results?</h3>
    <p class="text-mauve-700 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
      Your search lives in this browser session and goes away when it ends. An account keeps your
      Goodreads connection so you don't reconnect each visit, emails you when a waitlisted book comes
      free, and unlocks BookMooch trading for the books your library doesn't have.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/sign-up" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 bg-mauve-950 text-white text-sm font-medium rounded-full hover:bg-mauve-900 transition-colors">
        Create a free account
      </a>
      <button type="button" onclick="document.getElementById('save-results-card').remove()"
              class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 bg-mauve-950/10 text-mauve-950 text-sm font-medium rounded-full hover:bg-mauve-950/20 transition-colors">
        Maybe later
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/40">
    <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-2">See your reading patterns</h3>
    <p class="text-mauve-700 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
      The same shelf you just searched can tell you how your reading breaks down by publication
      year and your own ratings.
    </p>
    <div class="flex items-end gap-1.5 h-16 mb-5" aria-hidden="true">
      <% [40, 65, 30, 80, 55, 70, 45].each do |height| %>
        <div class="flex-1 rounded-t bg-gradient-to-t from-indigo-300 to-violet-400" style="height: <%= height %>%"></div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <a href="/sign-up" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 bg-mauve-950/10 text-mauve-950 text-sm font-medium rounded-full hover:bg-mauve-950/20 transition-colors">
      Unlock reading analytics
    </a>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Availability alerts need an email address, so an account (#1422). This
    replaced a Kit "notify me" form that never had anything behind it. %>
<div class="mt-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
  <div class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/40" id="alerts-signup">
    <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-2">Get an email when your books come free</h3>
    <p class="text-mauve-700 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
      Waitlists move, and libraries buy new books. With a free account, we'll check your libraries every
      morning and email you when a book on your list has a copy free. Only when something changes, and you can turn it off from any email.
    </p>
    <a href="/sign-up" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 bg-mauve-950 text-white text-sm font-medium rounded-full hover:bg-mauve-900 transition-colors">
      Create a free account for alerts
    </a>
  </div>
</div>
